        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Knaves',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Knaves is a fast-paced trick-taking card game for three players. It is an avoidance game where the primary objective is to gain points for tricks while avoiding the 'Knaves' (Jacks), which carry heavy negative scores. It blends traditional trick-play with the high-stakes risk-management found in games like Hearts.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dates to the early 1900s. It was popularized as a 'social' card game that simplified the complexity of Bridge or Whist, adding a more humorous 'hot potato' element with the penalty Jacks.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 players (standard).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards. Remove the Two of Spades to leave 51 cards (17 cards per player).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards. Remove the Two of Spades to leave 51 cards (17 cards per player).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Deal all 51 cards face-down. The player to the dealer's left leads the first trick.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
